WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
Привет, that means hello in Russian.

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:08.020
Welcome to привет, русский, эпизод 41, for 1610 июня 2026 года.

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.900
I'm Olya, and today we're going to learn some really fun Russian words.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:12.480
Ready?

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.600
Поехали, that means let's go.

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.060
Our word of the day is mid-vehid.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.720
Mi-yat-vehid, say it slowly with me.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.800
Mi-yat-vehid, it means bear.

00:00:22.440 --> 00:00:26.280
Imagine a big furry bear who knows exactly where the honey is hidden.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:29.140
That memory hook will help you remember the word.

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:30.940
Now use it in a sentence.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.660
Мидвьет-любит-мёт, the bear loves honey.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.020
Repeat after me.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.500
Мидвьет-любит.

00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:38.420
Now say it at normal speed.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:39.640
Мидвьет-любит.

00:00:40.180 --> 00:00:41.940
Let's build more animal words today.

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.520
Our first new word is птица.

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:46.580
Птица, it means bird.

00:00:47.160 --> 00:00:50.240
Птица sounds just like tweet, which is perfect for a bird.

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:51.420
Repeat after me.

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:52.200
Птица.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.780
Птица летает высоко.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:55.140
The bird flies high.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.600
Next we have Ри-ба, Ри-ба.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:58.660
That means fish.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.560
Picture a fish doing a little Ри-ба dance in the water.

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.560
Repeat after me.

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:03.260
Ри-ба.

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:04.820
Ри-ба плавает водя.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.360
The fish swims in the water.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:08.060
Now say, лошадь.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:09.040
Л-о-шад.

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:10.220
It means horse.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.820
Imagine the horse standing beside a low shed.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.100
Repeat after me.

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:15.320
Лошадь.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:17.400
Лошадь-бальшая и быстрее.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:18.980
The horse is big and fast.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:20.500
Here is корова.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.100
Корова, that means cow.

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.620
Think of a cow driving a car over a hill.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:25.880
Repeat after me.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:28.140
Корова, корова дает молоко.

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:29.480
The cow gives milk.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.940
Remember кошка from a few lessons ago?

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:32.660
Кошка.

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:33.920
It still means cat.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:35.500
Кошка спит на диване.

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.000
The cat sleeps on the sofa.

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:39.620
Remember собака, from a few lessons ago?

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:40.960
Са бака.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.280
It still means dog.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:43.900
Сабака бежит быстро.

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.080
The dog runs fast.

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.480
Remember mish from a few lessons ago.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:48.280
Майш.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.460
It still means mouse.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:51.500
Мышь маленькая и быстрее.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.060
The mouse is small and fast.

00:01:53.060 --> 00:01:55.840
We also learned le-tayet, le-tayet.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:01:57.780
It means flies or is flying.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.040
Let it sound like let it and let the bird fly.

00:02:01.440 --> 00:02:02.200
Repeat after me.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:03.340
Let-tayet.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.600
Ptitsa le-tayet, the bird flies.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.520
Now for a quick grammar bite.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.640
In Russian every noun has a gender.

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:13.020
Most animal names that end in a or ya are feminine.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:14.240
Корова is feminine.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:16.840
So we say anabalshaya, she is big.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.900
Мидвит ends in a consonant.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:19.860
It is masculine.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.880
So we say on lubit mute, he loves honey.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:24.280
Ptitsa ends in a.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:25.140
It is feminine.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:26.880
Анали-тayet, she flies.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.460
You do not need to memorize long rules.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:31.320
Just listen for the ending sound.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:32.840
In Russian fairy tales,

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:36.180
The midviet is often a strong but kind forest character.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:39.140
Children grow up hearing stories like Masha and the bear.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:42.280
The bear sometimes helps and sometimes tricks the little girl.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.420
It is a favorite tale across Russia.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.120
Time for our practice challenge.

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.020
If you are drawing,

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:50.480
color your favorite animal and say its Russian name three times.

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:52.340
If you see a dog or cat outside,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.600
quietly say sabaka or koscha,

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.100
then add a color you know.

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.040
Try it now with one word from today.

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.500
Want to know a secret about one of today's words?

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.080
The Russian word midvits and the English idea of honey eater

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.620
come from the same ancient root.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:07.780
Both mean the one who knows honey.

00:03:08.240 --> 00:03:11.000
Long ago, people avoided saying the real name of the bear.

00:03:11.420 --> 00:03:13.160
They worried it might bring bad luck.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.360
So they use this polite word instead.

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.700
Over centuries, it became midviet.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.120
It sounds nothing like the English word bear.

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:22.660
Yet it carries the same sweet golden meaning.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.220
Next time you hear honey,

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.460
remember it is cousins with midviet.

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:29.040
That connection will help you remember the word forever.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:29.840
Molladgets.

00:03:30.140 --> 00:03:31.240
That means well done.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:33.860
Remember every expert started as a beginner.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:35.960
Practice saying today's words out loud,

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:36.940
even just once.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.020
And you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.160
See you next time.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:41.760
Poka, that's Russian for buy.

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:43.660
And if you'd rather watch them listen,

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:46.160
find us on YouTube at AT NERA Are You.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:47.460
Links in the show notes.

